  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure will continue building south through eastern\nCanada and into the New England states will continue to permit\ndry and seasonable conditions through early next week. Some\nmorning fog remains possible this morning and again on Saturday\nmorning. The main forecast concern will be on Saturday and\nSunday morning when the high is both at its closest and\nstrongest to the area. This will allow for temperatures to drop\ninto the 30s for much of the area and some sheltered locations\nmay catch an upper 20 degree reading. Areas to widespread frost\nwill be expected from North Central Ohio to Northwest\nPennsylvania on Saturday and Sunday morning. Frost/freeze\nheadlines may be needed for areas still in the growing season\nprogram.",
